module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GlobalTypesOfModules
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Global types of modules under the comparison functor of a topology

Descent, Lemma 05VG compares the fifteen properties of modules of Modules on Sites,
Definitions 03DE, 03DL and 03ER across the equivalences
`QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh((Sch/S)_τ, 𝒪)` and `QCoh(𝒪_S) ⟶ QCoh(S_τ, 𝒪)`, `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕ᵃ`, of
Descent, Proposition 03DX, for `τ` any of the Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic and fppf
topologies: `𝓕` has the property if and only if `𝓕ᵃ` does, except possibly for local
freeness, and for coherence on the big sites.

The source splits its proof in two.  For the **global** properties — the seven of
Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE — it is "immediate", because those properties say that the
module is built from the structure sheaf by coproducts and cokernels, and the comparison is an
equivalence carrying the structure sheaf to the structure sheaf.  For the **local** properties
it goes through Modules on Sites, Lemma 03DN and the fpqc descent lemmas 05AZ, 05B0, 082U,
05B1 and 05B2.

**This file proves the first half, and only the first half.**  It makes "immediate" precise:
every one of the seven global properties is both preserved and reflected by a fully faithful,
coproduct-preserving functor between two categories of sheaves of modules which carries the
structure sheaf to the structure sheaf.  Nothing about schemes, about quasi-coherence or about
the topology enters, so the statements hold for *arbitrary* sites — in particular uniformly in
`τ`, and for the big and the small site alike.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.isColimitCofanMap` and
  `.isColimitCofanOfMap`: a family of global sections exhibits a module as a coproduct of
  copies of the structure sheaf if and only if its image does.  These are the two halves of
  the whole file; every property below is an application of one of them.
* `Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.mapFreeIso`: the comparison carries the free module on
  a type to the free module on the same type.
* `Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.generatingSectionsMap` and
  `.generatingSectionsOfMap`: generating families of global sections transported in both
  directions, with the index type unchanged.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.isFree_iff`,
  `.isFiniteFree_iff`,
  `.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff`,
  `.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff`,
  `.exists_isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff`,
  `.isPresentedByGlobalSections_iff` and
  `.isFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections_iff`: **Descent, Lemma 05VG for the seven global
  properties of Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE**, namely clauses (1) free, (2) finite free,
  (3) generated by global sections, (4) generated by `r` global sections, (5) generated by
  finitely many global sections, (6) having a global presentation and (7) having a finite
  global presentation.

## Implementation notes

Descent, Proposition 03DX — the equivalence itself — is **not** in the library: essential
surjectivity of `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕ᵃ` is not proved, so there is no functor here to instantiate these
statements at.  The comparison is therefore carried as explicit named hypotheses, and they are
*weaker* than an equivalence: a functor `Φ` between the two categories of sheaves of modules
which is full, faithful and preserves coproducts, together with an isomorphism
`Φ 𝒪₁ ≅ 𝒪₂`.  Essential surjectivity is never used.  Full faithfulness is used only through
`CategoryTheory.Limits.fullyFaithful_reflectsColimits`, which makes `Φ` reflect the colimits
that the properties are stated by, and through
`CategoryTheory.Functor.epi_of_epi_map` for the generation clauses.

Fullness is what the reverse implications cost, and they cost nothing more: a family of global
sections of `Φ 𝓕` is `Φ` of a family of global sections of `𝓕` because
`Φ 𝒪₁ ≅ 𝒪₂` identifies the two indexing objects and `Φ` is full on morphisms out of them.

Clauses (6) and (7) ask for two coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf, which the reverse
implication has to *produce* on the source side; `Φ` not being essentially surjective, they
cannot be preimages of the two given ones.  They are taken to be
`SheafOfModules.free`, whose comparison with the given ones is
`Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.mapFreeIso`, and the cokernel is then moved across by
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofork.isColimitOfIsos`.  This is why those two clauses, unlike
`SheafOfModules.IsPresentedByGlobalSections` itself, carry the sheafification hypotheses on the
source site that `SheafOfModules.free` needs.

The index types of clause (7) are `Fin n` and `Fin k`, which do not live in the universe of
sections, so the free modules used there are those on `ULift (Fin n)` and `ULift (Fin k)` and
their cofans are reindexed with
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv`; the resulting presentation is still
indexed by `Fin n` and `Fin k`, so no finiteness is lost.  Clause (7) needs no sheafification
hypothesis on the target site, its comparison isomorphism coming straight from
`Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.isColimitCofanMap`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison

universe w t v₁ u₁ v₂ u₂

variable {C₁ : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C₁] {J₁ : GrothendieckTopology C₁}
  {R₁ : Sheaf J₁ RingCat.{w}}
  {C₂ : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} C₂] {J₂ : GrothendieckTopology C₂}
  {R₂ : Sheaf J₂ RingCat.{w}}
  (Φ : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁ ⥤ SheafOfModules.{w} R₂)
  (u : Φ.obj (SheafOfModules.unit R₁) ≅ SheafOfModules.unit R₂)

/-- **A coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf maps to one.**  If a family of global
sections exhibits `F` as a coproduct of copies of `𝒪₁`, then the images of those sections,
read through `u`, exhibit `Φ F` as a coproduct of as many copies of `𝒪₂`.  This is the
colimit computation that the preservation half of every clause below rests on. -/
def isColimitCofanMap {B : Type t} [PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete B) Φ]
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁} (ι : ∀ _ : B, SheafOfModules.unit R₁ ⟶ F)
    (h : IsColimit (Cofan.mk F ι)) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk (Φ.obj F) fun b ↦ u.inv ≫ Φ.map (ι b)) :=
  ((IsColimit.precomposeHomEquiv
      (Discrete.natIso
        (F := Discrete.functor fun _ : B ↦ SheafOfModules.unit R₂)
        (G := Discrete.functor (fun _ : B ↦ SheafOfModules.unit R₁) ⋙ Φ)
        fun _ ↦ u.symm)
      (Φ.mapCocone (Cofan.mk F ι))).symm
    (isColimitOfPreserves Φ h))

/-- **Only a coproduct of copies of the structure sheaf maps to one.**  If a family of global
sections exhibits `Φ F` as a coproduct of copies of `𝒪₂`, then `Φ` being full those sections
come from global sections of `F`, and `Φ` being fully faithful it reflects the colimit, so
they exhibit `F` as a coproduct of as many copies of `𝒪₁`. -/
def isColimitCofanOfMap [Φ.Full] [Φ.Faithful] {B : Type t}
    {F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁} (κ : ∀ _ : B, SheafOfModules.unit R₂ ⟶ Φ.obj F)
    (h : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (Φ.obj F) κ)) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk F fun b ↦ Φ.preimage (u.hom ≫ κ b)) :=
  isColimitOfReflects Φ
    ((IsColimit.precomposeHomEquiv
        (Discrete.natIso
          (F := Discrete.functor fun _ : B ↦ SheafOfModules.unit R₂)
          (G := Discrete.functor (fun _ : B ↦ SheafOfModules.unit R₁) ⋙ Φ)
          fun _ ↦ u.symm)
        (Φ.mapCocone (Cofan.mk F fun b ↦ Φ.preimage (u.hom ≫ κ b))))
      (h.ofIsoColimit (Cocone.ext (Iso.refl _) (fun _ ↦ by simp))))

/-- A cokernel presentation of `Φ F` on modules isomorphic to images under `Φ` comes from a
cokernel presentation of `F`. -/
private theorem exists_isColimit_cokernelCofork_of_map [Φ.Full] [Φ.Faithful]
    {P Q F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁} {P' Q' : SheafOfModules.{w} R₂}
    (eP : Φ.obj P ≅ P') (eQ : Φ.obj Q ≅ Q')
    {a : Q' ⟶ P'} {b : P' ⟶ Φ.obj F} (hab : a ≫ b = 0)
    (hc : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab)) :
    ∃ (a' : Q ⟶ P) (b' : P ⟶ F) (hab' : a' ≫ b' = 0),
      Nonempty (IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b' hab')) := by
  have hab' : Φ.preimage (eQ.hom ≫ a ≫ eP.inv) ≫ Φ.preimage (eP.hom ≫ b) = 0 :=
    Φ.map_injective (by simp [hab])
  refine ⟨_, _, hab', ⟨isColimitOfReflects Φ ((isColimitMapCoconeCoforkEquiv' Φ hab').symm ?_)⟩⟩
  exact Cofork.isColimitOfIsos _ hc _ eQ.symm eP.symm (Iso.refl _) (by simp) (by simp) (by simp)

variable [Φ.Full] [Φ.Faithful] [PreservesColimitsOfSize.{w, w} Φ]

/-- `Φ` preserves colimits indexed by small categories in universe `0`. -/
local instance : PreservesColimitsOfSize.{0, 0} Φ := preservesColimitsOfSize_shrink _

include u in
/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE (1).**  A module is free if
and only if its image under the comparison is free: both sides are the assertion that some
family of global sections exhibits the module as a coproduct of copies of the structure
sheaf, and `Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.isColimitCofanMap` and
`.isColimitCofanOfMap` move such a family in the two directions without changing its index
type. -/
@[stacks 05VG "free; global properties only, and the comparison functor of 03DX hypothesised"]
theorem isFree_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁) : F.IsFree ↔ (Φ.obj F).IsFree := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨B, ι, ⟨h⟩⟩
    exact ⟨B, _, ⟨isColimitCofanMap Φ u ι h⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨B, κ, ⟨h⟩⟩
    exact ⟨B, _, ⟨isColimitCofanOfMap Φ u κ h⟩⟩

include u in
/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE (2).**  A module is finite
free if and only if its image under the comparison is finite free.  The ring and module
universes agreeing, `SheafOfModules.isFiniteFree_iff_exists_isColimit` reduces both sides to
a cofan with index type `Fin n`, and the same `n` works on both sides. -/
@[stacks 05VG
  "finite free; global properties only, and the comparison functor of 03DX hypothesised"]
theorem isFiniteFree_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁) :
    SheafOfModules.IsFiniteFree R₁ F ↔ SheafOfModules.IsFiniteFree R₂ (Φ.obj F) := by
  rw [SheafOfModules.isFiniteFree_iff_exists_isColimit,
    SheafOfModules.isFiniteFree_iff_exists_isColimit]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨n, ι, ⟨h⟩⟩
    exact ⟨n, _, ⟨isColimitCofanMap Φ u ι h⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨n, κ, ⟨h⟩⟩
    exact ⟨n, _, ⟨isColimitCofanOfMap Φ u κ h⟩⟩

section Generation

variable [HasWeakSheafify J₁ AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J₁.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [HasWeakSheafify J₂ AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J₂.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- **The free comparison.**  The comparison carries the free module on a type to the free
module on the same type: both are coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf indexed by that
type, and `Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.isColimitCofanMap` says the second is the image
of the first. -/
def mapFreeIso (B : Type w) :
    SheafOfModules.free (R := R₂) B ≅ Φ.obj (SheafOfModules.free (R := R₁) B) :=
  (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan B).coconePointUniqueUpToIso
    (isColimitCofanMap Φ u _ (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan B))

/-- A generating family of global sections, transported to a generating family of global
sections of the image indexed by the same type: the generating map is the free comparison
followed by the image of the original generating map, an epimorphism because `Φ` preserves
epimorphisms. -/
def generatingSectionsMap {F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁} (σ : F.GeneratingSections) :
    (Φ.obj F).GeneratingSections where
  I := σ.I
  s := (Φ.obj F).freeHomEquiv ((mapFreeIso Φ u σ.I).hom ≫ Φ.map σ.π)
  epi := by
    have : Φ.PreservesEpimorphisms := inferInstance
    simp only [Equiv.symm_apply_apply, epi_comp_iff_of_epi]
    infer_instance

/-- A generating family of global sections of the image, transported back to a generating
family of global sections indexed by the same type: the generating map is the preimage under
`Φ` of the free comparison followed by the original generating map, an epimorphism because a
fully faithful functor reflects epimorphisms. -/
def generatingSectionsOfMap {F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁} (σ : (Φ.obj F).GeneratingSections) :
    F.GeneratingSections where
  I := σ.I
  s := F.freeHomEquiv (Φ.preimage ((mapFreeIso Φ u σ.I).inv ≫ σ.π))
  epi := by
    simp only [Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
    refine Φ.epi_of_epi_map ?_
    rw [Φ.map_preimage]
    infer_instance

include u in
/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE (3).**  A module is generated
by global sections if and only if its image under the comparison is. -/
@[stacks 05VG "generated by global sections; global properties only, and the comparison \
functor of 03DX hypothesised"]
theorem isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁) :
    F.IsGeneratedByGlobalSections ↔ (Φ.obj F).IsGeneratedByGlobalSections :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨generatingSectionsMap Φ u h.some⟩, fun h ↦ ⟨generatingSectionsOfMap Φ u h.some⟩⟩

include u in
/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE (4).**  A module is generated
by `r` global sections if and only if its image under the comparison is: the transported
generating family is indexed by the same type, so the same `r` works. -/
@[stacks 05VG "generated by r global sections; global properties only, and the comparison \
functor of 03DX hypothesised"]
theorem isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁) (r : ℕ) :
    F.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r ↔
      (Φ.obj F).IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r :=
  ⟨fun h ↦ ⟨generatingSectionsMap Φ u h.choose, h.choose_spec⟩,
    fun h ↦ ⟨generatingSectionsOfMap Φ u h.choose, h.choose_spec⟩⟩

include u in
/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE (5).**  A module is generated
by finitely many global sections if and only if its image under the comparison is. -/
@[stacks 05VG "generated by finitely many global sections; global properties only, and the \
comparison functor of 03DX hypothesised"]
theorem exists_isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁) :
    (∃ r : ℕ, F.IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r) ↔
      ∃ r : ℕ, (Φ.obj F).IsGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard r :=
  exists_congr (isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_iff Φ u F)

include u in
/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE (6).**  A module has a global
presentation if and only if its image under the comparison has one.

The preservation half maps the two coproducts and the cokernel across.  The reverse half
cannot take preimages of the two given coproducts, `Φ` not being essentially surjective; it
takes `SheafOfModules.free` on the two given index types instead, compares them with the given
coproducts through `Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison.mapFreeIso`, and moves the cokernel
across that comparison with `CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofork.isColimitOfIsos` before reflecting
it along `Φ`.  The two index types are unchanged. -/
@[stacks 05VG "global presentation; global properties only, and the comparison functor of \
03DX hypothesised"]
theorem isPresentedByGlobalSections_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁) :
    F.IsPresentedByGlobalSections ↔ (Φ.obj F).IsPresentedByGlobalSections := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨I, K, P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, ⟨hc⟩⟩
    exact ⟨I, K, Φ.obj P, Φ.obj Q, _, _,
      ⟨isColimitCofanMap Φ u ι hP⟩, ⟨isColimitCofanMap Φ u κ hQ⟩,
      Φ.map a, Φ.map b, _, ⟨isColimitCoforkMapOfIsColimit' Φ hab hc⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨I, K, P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, ⟨hc⟩⟩
    have eP : Φ.obj (SheafOfModules.free (R := R₁) I) ≅ P :=
      (mapFreeIso Φ u I).symm ≪≫
        (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan I).coconePointUniqueUpToIso hP
    have eQ : Φ.obj (SheafOfModules.free (R := R₁) K) ≅ Q :=
      (mapFreeIso Φ u K).symm ≪≫
        (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan K).coconePointUniqueUpToIso hQ
    obtain ⟨a', b', hab', hc'⟩ := exists_isColimit_cokernelCofork_of_map Φ eP eQ hab hc
    exact ⟨I, K, _, _, _, _, ⟨SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan I⟩,
      ⟨SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan K⟩, a', b', hab', hc'⟩


omit [HasWeakSheafify J₂ AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J₂.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] in
include u in
/-- **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DE (7).**  A module has a finite
global presentation if and only if its image under the comparison has one, with the same two
finite index types `Fin n` and `Fin k`.

Those index types do not live in the universe of sections, so the two coproducts the reverse
half builds are the free modules on `ULift (Fin n)` and `ULift (Fin k)`, with their cofans
reindexed by `CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv`; the presentation produced is
still indexed by `Fin n` and `Fin k`, so the finiteness is not weakened. -/
@[stacks 05VG "finite global presentation; global properties only, and the comparison functor \
of 03DX hypothesised"]
theorem isFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections_iff (F : SheafOfModules.{w} R₁) :
    F.IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections ↔
      (Φ.obj F).IsFinitelyPresentedByGlobalSections := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨n, k, P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, ⟨hc⟩⟩
    exact ⟨n, k, Φ.obj P, Φ.obj Q, _, _,
      ⟨isColimitCofanMap Φ u ι hP⟩, ⟨isColimitCofanMap Φ u κ hQ⟩,
      Φ.map a, Φ.map b, _, ⟨isColimitCoforkMapOfIsColimit' Φ hab hc⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨n, k, P, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hP⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, ⟨hc⟩⟩
    have hfn : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (SheafOfModules.free (R := R₁) (ULift.{w} (Fin n)))
        fun i : Fin n ↦
          (SheafOfModules.freeCofan (R := R₁) (ULift.{w} (Fin n))).inj (Equiv.ulift.symm i)) :=
      (Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv (ε := Equiv.ulift.symm)
        (SheafOfModules.freeCofan (R := R₁) (ULift.{w} (Fin n))))
        (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan _)
    have hfk : IsColimit (Cofan.mk (SheafOfModules.free (R := R₁) (ULift.{w} (Fin k)))
        fun i : Fin k ↦
          (SheafOfModules.freeCofan (R := R₁) (ULift.{w} (Fin k))).inj (Equiv.ulift.symm i)) :=
      (Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv (ε := Equiv.ulift.symm)
        (SheafOfModules.freeCofan (R := R₁) (ULift.{w} (Fin k))))
        (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan _)
    have eP : Φ.obj (SheafOfModules.free (R := R₁) (ULift.{w} (Fin n))) ≅ P :=
      (isColimitCofanMap Φ u _ hfn).coconePointUniqueUpToIso hP
    have eQ : Φ.obj (SheafOfModules.free (R := R₁) (ULift.{w} (Fin k))) ≅ Q :=
      (isColimitCofanMap Φ u _ hfk).coconePointUniqueUpToIso hQ
    obtain ⟨a', b', hab', hc'⟩ := exists_isColimit_cokernelCofork_of_map Φ eP eQ hab hc
    exact ⟨n, k, _, _, _, _, ⟨hfn⟩, ⟨hfk⟩, a', b', hab', hc'⟩

end Generation

end Stacks.Sheaves.GlobalTypeComparison

end
